# Demo isolation — do not leak showcase chrome into shared code

Demo visual primitives use shared generic classes such as `.section-panel`, `.panel-title`, `.panel-hint`, `.panel-row`, `.panel-inline`, and `.panel-grid`. Only catalogue-specific wiring or visualisation in `demo.html` / `app/demo.js` may remain **`demo-*`** prefixed.

## Never

- Reference `demo-*` class names from `app/shell/`, `app/utils/`, or other shared modules
- Add selectors for `demo-*` in shared CSS that shell/components depend on (prefer generic names under `app/css/`)
- Teach sticky, page-nav, or other shell behaviour to only work with demo-prefixed markup

## When demo needs layout that shell also uses

1. Give it a **generic** name (e.g. `.content-section`, `.content-tier`, `.section-title`, `.panel-split`)
2. Document it in `USAGE.md` as a reusable layout pattern
3. Use that generic name in both the demo and shared JS/CSS

## Allowed `demo-*` usage

- Catalogue-specific classes that exist only in `demo.html` / `app/demo.js` and their demo-only CSS (for example `.demo-colour-*` and `.demo-banner-*`)
- Element ids like `demo-combobox` for demo wiring
